# (after 0528) host/audren: a renderer the game itself opens as CPU + manual is left to the game (no host render thread, capture or catch-up)
#
# Upstream:  https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/commit/b2d41ac5759357f0f132adc9b5c59038d32943e6  ("host/audren: leave explicit CPU/manual renderers to the game (issue #3212)")
#            author seedds, 2026-11-23 03:13 +0800; Co-authored-by: Damien Frigewski
# Licence:   MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 seedds (nxnative LICENSE); ported from seedds/nxnative, MIT. The attribution above is kept as the licence asks.
#
# Why: games that open nn::audio::AudioRenderer in CPU + manual mode (renderingDevice 1, executionMode 1) drive ExecuteAudioRendererRendering themselves (often into a circular buffer
#   sink and a direct AudioOut); the host still started render_main, captured the DeviceSink in ar_exec and ran catch-up renders and 50 ms waits in Update (upstream issue #3212).
# WHAT IT CHANGES (dm/host/hle_audren.c; tests t_audren_work, t_audio): manual is kept per renderer (ar_t.manual): the caller's parameter goes through as it is, no render thread is started or joined,
#   Update / ImplExec / Exec forward to the SDK's originals, unbound manual slots are bound apart from the host-driven ones so both kinds coexist.
# Adapted: ar_open by hand (this tree's slot reset keeps cq_mu / cq_cv and has render_active: a manual renderer starts with render_active 0, so the teardown does not wait for a thread).
#   0453's real-time policy and 0454's tails apply to host-driven renderers only, as before.
# Games: games with an explicit CPU / manual renderer (issue #3212). Switches: none.
#   t_audio's render-thread teardown race (part 3, a test of the base tree) opened its renderer as CPU + manual: it now opens it as DSP / auto (device 0, mode 0), the host-driven
#   renderer whose render_main it is about; as CPU + manual it would have no render thread to race.
# Tests (M1 Pro): t_audren_work, t_audren_layout, t_audio (host-unit run of HOST_TESTS). NOT run on a device.
# Shader chain: not touched (b24b25240cad; scripts/build-host.sh checks it).
# Apply with: patch -p1, to the tree out-stage/out-engine/engine + engine-patches/0401..0528, in the order of the numbers of this folder (scripts/build-host.sh does).

